   "text": "Sample Size for a Proportion\nTo estimate a proportion with margin of error E at 95% confidence use n = z squared * p * (1 - p) / E squared. When no prior estimate of p exists use p = 0.5, which gives the largest required sample. With z = 1.96, p = 0.5 and E = 0.05 the result is 384.16, so round up to a sample of 385 respondents.",
